s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T12:03:06Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T12:03:06Z","body":"Same issue here on **Airflow 3.3.1** (official chart 1.22.0, PostgreSQL 17).\nI found the cause and was able to reproduce it on a fresh install.\n\n### Root cause\n\nThe rows that block the delete are **task instances that never started**: `state IS NULL`, `start_date IS NULL`.\nThey belong to a DAG that is paused and later becomes stale (its file was removed).\n\n1. The `task_instance` cleanup filters on `start_date`.\n   It is NULL for these rows, so they are never eligible.\n   The same happens to their `dag_run`, which stays `queued` with `start_date` NULL.\n2. The `dag` cleanup picks stale DAGs by `last_parsed_time`.\n   Deleting those rows cascades to `dag_version` (`dag_version_dag_id_fkey ... ON DELETE CASCADE`).\n3. `task_instance_dag_version_id_fkey` is `ON DELETE RESTRICT`, so the whole `DELETE FROM dag` fails.\n   Nothing checks whether the DAG's versions are still referenced before deleting.\n\nOnce a DAG reaches this state, every later run of `db clean` fails on the `dag` table.\nEach failed run also leaves an `_airflow_deleted__dag__*` table behind.\n\nIn production, 76 DAGs were eligible for deletion.\n2 of them had 7 task instances in this state, and that was enough to block the `dag` table for every run.\n\n### Reproduction (fresh 3.3.1 DB, chart 1.22.0, `dags_are_paused_at_creation=True`)\n\n1. Add this DAG file and wait until it is parsed. It is created paused.\n\n   ```python\n   from datetime import datetime\n   from airflow.providers.standard.operators.empty import EmptyOperator\n   from airflow.sdk import DAG\n\n   with DAG(dag_id=\"repro_never_started\", schedule=None,\n            start_date=datetime(2026, 1, 1), catchup=False):\n       EmptyOperator(task_id=\"a\") >> EmptyOperator(task_id=\"b\")\n   ```\n\n2. Trigger it while it is still paused: `airflow dags trigger repro_never_started`.\n   The result is a `dag_run` with `state=queued` and `start_date` NULL, plus 2 task instances with `state` NULL and `start_date` NULL.\n3. Delete the DAG file and wait for `is_stale = true`.\n4. Run `airflow db clean --clean-before-timestamp \"$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S)\" --yes --verbose`:\n\n   ```\n   Checking table task_instance\n   Found 0 rows meeting deletion criteria.\n   ...\n   Checking table dag_run\n   Found 0 rows meeting deletion criteria.\n   Checking table dag_version\n   Found 0 rows meeting deletion criteria.\n   Checking table dag\n   Found 1 rows meeting deletion criteria.\n   Moving data to table _airflow_deleted__dag__20261013115501\n   sqlalchemy.exc.IntegrityError: (psycopg2.errors.ForeignKeyViolation) update or delete on table \"dag_version\" violates foreign key constraint \"task_instance_dag_version_id_fkey\" on table \"task_instance\"\n   DETAIL:  Key (id)=(01a1351c-...) is still referenced from table \"task_instance\".\n   [SQL: DELETE FROM dag USING _airflow_deleted__dag__20261013115501 WHERE dag.dag_id = _airflow_deleted__dag__20261013115501.dag_id]\n   ```\n\n### Workaround (verified)\n\nDelete the never-started task instances of the stale DAGs, then run `db clean` again.\nWith this, the run completes with exit 0:\n\n```sql\nDELETE FROM task_instance ti\nUSING dag_version v, dag d\nWHERE v.id = ti.dag_version_id AND d.dag_id = v.dag_id\n  AND d.is_stale AND d.last_parsed_time < '<clean_before_ts>'\n  AND ti.start_date IS NULL;\n```\n\nThe `queued` dag_run is left behind as an orphan, because nothing cleans runs with a NULL `start_date`.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/comments/6145101819/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"fernando-luiz-effecti","id":158169645,"node_id":"U_kgDOCW16LQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/158169645?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti","html_url":"https://github.com/fernando-luiz-effecti","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fernando-luiz-effecti/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"actor":{"login":"ucaeon","id":149305644,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOY5LA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149305644?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ucaeon","html_url":"https://github.com/ucaeon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ucaeon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ucaeon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ucaeon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ucaeon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ucaeon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https: